<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/A6NGE7">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Putative 2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-ureidoimidazoline decarboxylase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_URAD_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_A6NGE7" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">URAD_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Parahox neighbor</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ureidoimidazoline (2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-) decarboxylase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OHCU decarboxylase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">URAD</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PRHOXNB</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">4.1.1.97</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">URAD_HUMAN Reviewed; 173 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the stereoselective decarboxylation of 2-oxo-4-hydroxy-4-carboxy-5-ureidoimidazoline (OHCU) to (S)-allantoin.{ECO:0000305}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=5-hydroxy-2-oxo-4-ureido-2,5-dihydro-1H-imidazole-5-carboxylate + H(+) = (S)-allantoin + CO2; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:26301,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:15678, ChEBI:CHEBI:16526,ChEBI:CHEBI:58639; EC=4.1.1.97;PATHWAY: Purine metabolism; urate degradation; (S)-allantoin fromurate: step 3/3.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Peroxisome {ECO:0000305}.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Apparently not expressed.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the OHCU decarboxylase family.{ECO:0000305}.CAUTION: Could be the product of a pseudogene. In primates thegenes coding for the enzymes for the degradation of uric acid wereinactivated and converted to pseudogenes (PubMed:16462750).{ECO:0000305|PubMed:16462750}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

