<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q9UJA2">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Cardiolipin synthase (CMP-forming)</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9UJA2" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_CRLS1_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CRLS1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.8.41</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C20orf155</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Protein GCD10 homolog</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CLS1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CLS</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CRLS1</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_12187_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9UJA2_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the synthesis of cardiolipin (CL)(diphosphatidylglycerol) by specifically transferring aphosphatidyl group from CDP-diacylglycerol to phosphatidylglycerol(PG). CL is a key phospholipid in mitochondrial membranes andplays important roles in maintaining the functional integrity anddynamics of mitochondria under both optimal and stress conditions.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547353, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16678169}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1&apos;-sn-glycerol) + a CDP-1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol = a cardiolipin + CMP + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:32931, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:58332,ChEBI:CHEBI:60377, ChEBI:CHEBI:62237, ChEBI:CHEBI:64716;EC=2.7.8.41; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:16678169};COFACTOR:Name=a divalent metal cation; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:60240;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:16678169};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:pH dependence:Optimum pH is 8.2. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16678169};SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion inner membrane{ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547353}; Multi-pass membrane protein{ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547353}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q9UJA2-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9UJA2-2; Sequence=VSP_041398, VSP_041399;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in tissues such as heart,skeletal muscle and liver. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16547353}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the CDP-alcohol phosphatidyltransferaseclass-I family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_54675</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference90101</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CRLS1_HUMAN Reviewed; 301 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_006723642</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

