 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-oxoacyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] synthase, mitochondrial</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9NWU1" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_OXSM_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OXSM_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OXSM</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.3.1.41</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-ketoacyl-ACP synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference128912</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OXSM_HUMAN Reviewed; 459 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ra.cs.uni-tuebingen.de/software/KEGGtranslator/EC231179.eref</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9NWU1_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: May play a role in the biosynthesis of lipoic acid aswell as longer chain fatty acids required for optimalmitochondrial function. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a fatty acyl-[ACP] + H(+) + malonyl-[ACP] = a 3-oxoacyl-[ACP] + CO2 + holo-[ACP]; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:22836, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9623, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9685, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:9916, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14125, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:16526,ChEBI:CHEBI:64479, ChEBI:CHEBI:78449, ChEBI:CHEBI:78776,ChEBI:CHEBI:138651; EC=2.3.1.41;ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by cerulenin.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=3.9 uM for C4-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};KM=1.9 uM for C6-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};KM=10.9 uM for C8-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};KM=1.8 uM for C10-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};KM=9.5 uM for C12-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};KM=50.8 uM for C14-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=129 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C4-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=241 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C6-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=271 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C8-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=364 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C10-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=1045 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C12-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Vmax=115 nmol/min/mg enzyme toward C14-[acyl-carrier-protein]{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256};Note=The highest catalytic efficiency is observed for C10-[acyl-carrier-protein].;PATHWAY: Lipid metabolism; fatty acid biosynthesis.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q9NWU1-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9NWU1-2; Sequence=VSP_041671;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed. Higher expression in heart,skeletal muscle, liver and kidney which contain high levels ofactive mitochondria. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15668256}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the thiolase-like superfamily. Beta-ketoacyl-ACP synthases family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

