 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q5SPY7</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: In the nervous system, could hydrolyze ATP and othernucleotides to regulate purinergic neurotransmission. HydrolyzesADP only to a marginal extent. The order of activity withdifferent substrates is ATP &gt; GTP &gt; CTP = ITP &gt; UTP &gt;&gt; ADP = UDP.COFACTOR:Name=Ca(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29108;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10510450};Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10510450};SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Long: Cell membrane; Multi-passmembrane protein.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Short: Endoplasmic reticulummembrane; Multi-pass membrane protein.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform gamma: Endoplasmic reticulummembrane; Multi-pass membrane protein.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=Long; Synonyms=alpha;IsoId=Q9Y5L3-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=Short; Synonyms=beta;IsoId=Q9Y5L3-2; Sequence=VSP_003610;Note=Catalytically inactive.;Name=gamma;IsoId=Q9Y5L3-3; Sequence=VSP_003610, VSP_053548;Note=Catalytically inactive.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Brain, placenta, skeletal muscle, kidney,pancreas, heart, ovary, testis, colon, small intestine, prostateand pancreas. No expression in adult thymus, spleen, lung, liverand peripheral blood leukocytes.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the GDA1/CD39 NTPase family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_03600_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ENTP2_HUMAN Reviewed; 495 AA.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

