 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Lysosomal L-amino-acid oxidase with highest specificactivity with phenylalanine. May play a role in lysosomal antigenprocessing and presentation (By similarity). {ECO:0000250}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=an L-alpha-amino acid + H2O + O2 = a 2-oxocarboxylate +H2O2 + NH4(+); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:13781, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:15379, ChEBI:CHEBI:16240, ChEBI:CHEBI:28938,ChEBI:CHEBI:35179, ChEBI:CHEBI:59869; EC=1.4.3.2;COFACTOR:Name=FAD; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57692; Evidence={ECO:0000250};SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform 1: Lysosome {ECO:0000250}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform 2: Lysosome {ECO:0000250}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative promoter usage, Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q96RQ9-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=IL4I1_2;IsoId=Q96RQ9-2; Sequence=VSP_017173;Note=Uses the promoter of the upstream NUP62 gene and shares thefirst 2 non-coding exons with NUP62.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Isoform 1 is primarily found in immunetissues. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12031486}.INDUCTION: By IL4/interleukin-4.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the flavin monoamine oxidase family. FIG1subfamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAB84923.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=CAI54291.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=CAI54292.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=CAI54293.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

