<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q9BVG9">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_839187cb30d970d4d36ca8b05b3cefea" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_04ac4c1f5b0e9101115b42dd71cb641e" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_96580058de1cc0e17a1a6dda60090e00" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_25a159b4b863851b594f865bedf23c06" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_cf6cea66c374226f06f675eb09c6ee17" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Phosphatidylserine synthase 2</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_PTDSS2_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9BVG9" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PTSS2_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Serine-exchange enzyme II</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PTDSS2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.8.29</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PSS2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PtdSer synthase 2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PSS-2</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_011518695</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_81490</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes a base-exchange reaction in which the polarhead group of phosphatidylethanolamine (PE) or phosphatidylcholine(PC) is replaced by L-serine. PTDSS2 is specific forphosphatatidylethanolamine and does not act onphosphatidylcholine.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoethanolamine + L-serine= 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-L-serine + ethanolamine;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:27606, ChEBI:CHEBI:33384, ChEBI:CHEBI:57262,ChEBI:CHEBI:57603, ChEBI:CHEBI:64612; EC=2.7.8.29;ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited in both the MAM and the ER per seby ethanolamine. Requires calcium ions.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:19014349}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=120 uM for serine (in the presence of 1 mM PE){ECO:0000269|PubMed:19014349};Vmax=0.57 mmol/h/mg enzyme {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19014349};pH dependence:Optimum pH is around 7.5. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19014349};PATHWAY: Phospholipid metabolism; phosphatidylserine biosynthesis.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane{ECO:0000250}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000250}.Note=Highly enriched in the mitochondria-associated membrane(MAM). {ECO:0000250}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the phosphatidyl serine synthase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_81490</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9BVG9_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference93417</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PTSS2_HUMAN Reviewed; 487 AA.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

