 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methionine adenosyltransferase 2 subunit beta</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_MAT2B_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9NZL9" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAT2B_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAT II beta</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Putative dTDP-4-keto-6-deoxy-D-glucose 4-reductase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAT2B</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methionine adenosyltransferase II beta</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TGR</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAT2B_HUMAN Reviewed; 334 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q9NZL9_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_27430</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.humanmetabolism.org/#ref_http://www.humanmetabolism.org/#protein_MAT2B</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_27430</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_05701_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference82165</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_A0A140VJP2_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot.isoform/Q9NZL9-2</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Regulatory subunit of S-adenosylmethionine synthetase 2,an enzyme that catalyzes the formation of S-adenosylmethioninefrom methionine and ATP. Regulates MAT2A catalytic activity bychanging its kinetic properties, increasing its affinity for L-methionine (PubMed:10644686, PubMed:23189196, PubMed:25075345).Can bind NADP (in vitro) (PubMed:23189196, PubMed:23425511).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10644686, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23189196,ECO:0000269|PubMed:23425511, ECO:0000269|PubMed:25075345}.PATHWAY: Amino-acid biosynthesis; S-adenosyl-L-methioninebiosynthesis; S-adenosyl-L-methionine from L-methionine: step 1/1.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10644686, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23189196,ECO:0000269|PubMed:25075345}.SUBUNIT: Heterotrimer; composed of a catalytic MAT2A homodimerthat binds one regulatory MAT2B chain (PubMed:10644686,PubMed:23189196). Heterohexamer; composed of a central, catalyticMAT2A homotetramer flanked on either side by a regulatory MAT2Bchain (PubMed:25075345). NADP binding increases the affinity forMAT2A (PubMed:23189196). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10644686,ECO:0000269|PubMed:25075345, ECO:0000305|PubMed:23189196}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=5;Name=1;IsoId=Q9NZL9-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9NZL9-2; Sequence=VSP_025534;Name=3;IsoId=Q9NZL9-3; Sequence=VSP_025538, VSP_025539;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=4;IsoId=Q9NZL9-4; Sequence=VSP_025534, VSP_025540;Name=5;IsoId=Q9NZL9-5; Sequence=VSP_025535, VSP_025536, VSP_025537;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10644686, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11337507}.MISCELLANEOUS: Its expression in hepatoma cell lines may lead toincrease DNA synthesis and thereby participate in cellproliferation.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the dTDP-4-dehydrorhamnose reductasefamily. MAT2B subfamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAG39296.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

