 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Maintains high levels of reduced glutathione in thecytosol.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2 glutathione + NADP(+) = glutathione disulfide + H(+) +NADPH; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11740, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57783, ChEBI:CHEBI:57925, ChEBI:CHEBI:58297,ChEBI:CHEBI:58349; EC=1.8.1.7;COFACTOR:Name=FAD; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57692;Note=Binds 1 FAD per subunit.;SUBUNIT: Homodimer; disulfide-linked.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:8626496}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Mitochondrial: Mitochondrion.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Isoform Cytoplasmic: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing, Alternative initiation; Named isoforms=5;Name=Mitochondrial;IsoId=P00390-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=Cytoplasmic;IsoId=P00390-2; Sequence=VSP_018972;Note=Produced by alternative initiation of isoformMitochondrial.;Name=2; Synonyms=delta8;IsoId=P00390-3; Sequence=VSP_042908;Name=3; Synonyms=delta9;IsoId=P00390-4; Sequence=VSP_042909;Note=Expressed at very high levels in peripheral blood.;Name=4; Synonyms=delta8+9;IsoId=P00390-5; Sequence=VSP_042908, VSP_042909;DOMAIN: Each subunit can be divided into 4 domains that areconsecutive along the polypeptide chain. Domains 1 and 2 bind FADand NADPH, respectively. Domain 4 forms the interface.MISCELLANEOUS: The active site is a redox-active disulfide bond.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class-I pyridine nucleotide-disulfideoxidoreductase family. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAP88037.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};WEB RESOURCE: Name=NIEHS-SNPs;URL=&quot;http://egp.gs.washington.edu/data/gsr/&quot;;WEB RESOURCE: Name=Wikipedia; Note=Glutathione reductase entry;URL=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glutathione_reductase&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_2936</bp:comment>
