 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Has a threefold preference for the hydrolysis of ATPover ADP.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a ribonucleoside 5&apos;-triphosphate + 2 H2O = aribonucleoside 5&apos;-phosphate + 2 H(+) + 2 phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:36795, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:43474, ChEBI:CHEBI:58043, ChEBI:CHEBI:61557;EC=3.6.1.5;COFACTOR:Name=Ca(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29108;Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Membrane {ECO:0000305}; Multi-pass membraneprotein {ECO:0000305}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=O75355-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=O75355-2; Sequence=VSP_054237;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in adult brain, pancreas, spleen andprostate. Moderate or low expression is seen in most tissues. Notexpressed in liver and peripheral blood leukocytes.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the GDA1/CD39 NTPase family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
