 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Interconversion of serine and glycine (PubMed:8505317,PubMed:24698160). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160,ECO:0000269|PubMed:8505317}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=(6R)-5,10-methylene-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + glycine +H2O = (6S)-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrofolate + L-serine;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:15481, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15636,ChEBI:CHEBI:33384, ChEBI:CHEBI:57305, ChEBI:CHEBI:57453;EC=2.1.2.1; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160,ECO:0000269|PubMed:8505317};COFACTOR:Name=pyridoxal 5&apos;-phosphate; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:597326;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160,ECO:0000269|PubMed:25619277, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9753690};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by tetrahydrofolate concentrationsabove 40 uM. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.18 mM for L-serine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160};KM=5.2 uM for tetrahydrofolate {ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160};PATHWAY: One-carbon metabolism; tetrahydrofolate interconversion.{ECO:0000305|PubMed:24698160}.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer (PubMed:24698160, PubMed:25619277,PubMed:9753690). Identified in complex with ABRAXAS2 and the othersubunits of the BRISC complex, at least composed of ABRAXAS2,BRCC3/BRCC36, BABAM2 and BABAM1/NBA1 (PubMed:24075985).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:24075985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24698160,ECO:0000269|PubMed:25619277, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9753690}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=4;Name=1;IsoId=P34896-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P34896-2; Sequence=VSP_006095;Note=Contains a N6-acetyllysine at position 271.{ECO:0000244|PubMed:19608861};Name=3;IsoId=P34896-3; Sequence=VSP_006096;Name=4;IsoId=P34896-4; Sequence=VSP_054610;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;MISCELLANEOUS: In eukaryotes there are two forms of the enzymes: acytosolic one and a mitochondrial one. {ECO:0000305}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the SHMT family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
