 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Phosphoglycerate kinase 2</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_PGK2_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P07205" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PGK2_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Phosphoglycerate kinase, testis specific</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.2.3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PGK2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PGKB</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PGK2_HUMAN Reviewed; 417 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference102958</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Essential for sperm motility and male fertility(PubMed:26677959). Not required for the completion ofspermatogenesis (By similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P09041,ECO:0000269|PubMed:26677959}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-phospho-D-glycerate + ATP = 3-phospho-D-glyceroylphosphate + ADP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:14801, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616,ChEBI:CHEBI:57604, ChEBI:CHEBI:58272, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216;EC=2.7.2.3;PATHWAY: Carbohydrate degradation; glycolysis; pyruvate from D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate: step 2/5.SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P09041}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm {ECO:0000250}.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Mainly found in round spermatids. Localized onthe principle piece in the sperm (at protein level). Testis-specific. Expression significantly decreased in the testis ofelderly men. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:26677959}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the phosphoglycerate kinase family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Wikipedia; Note=Phosphoglycerate kinase entry;URL=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphoglycerate_kinase&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_620061</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_5232</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

