 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the reversible isomerization betweenhydroxypyruvate and 2-hydroxy-3-oxopropanoate (also termedtartronate semialdehyde). {ECO:0000250}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-hydroxypyruvate = 2-hydroxy-3-oxopropanoate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11952, ChEBI:CHEBI:17180, ChEBI:CHEBI:57978;EC=5.3.1.22;ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=4;Name=1;IsoId=Q5T013-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q5T013-2; Sequence=VSP_025986, VSP_025987;Name=3;IsoId=Q5T013-3; Sequence=VSP_025987;Name=4;IsoId=Q5T013-4; Sequence=VSP_025986;INDUCTION: Up-regulated by exposure to 7,8-Dihydroxy-9,10-epoxy-7,8,9,10-tetrahydrobenzo[a]pyrene (BPDE) after which is found inthe culture medium of amniotic epithelial cells.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:19722193}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the hyi family. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAH06140.1; Type=Frameshift; Positions=271; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=AAH19041.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally extended.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=AAV84474.1; Type=Frameshift; Positions=215, 228, 232, 238; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_11039_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HYI_HUMAN Reviewed; 277 AA.</bp:comment>
