 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHEBI:28102</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">(1,4-alpha-D-Glucosyl)n</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1,4-alpha-D-Glucan</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">(1,4-alpha-D-Glucosyl)n+1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">4-{(1,4)-alpha-D-Glucosyl}(n-1)-D-glucose</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">is_a CHEBI:37163</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3SmallMoleculeReference85654</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">has_role CHEBI:76924</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">has_role CHEBI:75771</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A glucan composed of unbranched chains of D-glucopyranose residues in alpha(1-&gt;4) glycosidic linkage. The number of repeated glucose subunits (n) is usually in the range of 300 to 3000, but can be many thousands. One of the two components of starch (the other, 70-80%, being amylopectin). Cf. linear maltodextrin, in which the chain length is typically between 3 and 17 glucose units.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.drugbank.ca/#ref_DB15216</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">has_role CHEBI:76971</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ra.cs.uni-tuebingen.de/software/KEGGtranslator/cpdC00718.eref</bp:comment>
</bp:SmallMoleculeReference>

<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q2QD12">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ribulose-phosphate 3-epimerase-like protein 1</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_RPEL1_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q2QD12" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RPEL1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5.1.3.1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RPEL1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ribulose-5-phosphate-3-epimerase-like protein 1</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RPEL1_HUMAN Reviewed; 228 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the reversible epimerization of D-ribulose 5-phosphate to D-xylulose 5-phosphate. {ECO:0000250}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=D-ribulose 5-phosphate = D-xylulose 5-phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:13677, ChEBI:CHEBI:57737, ChEBI:CHEBI:58121;EC=5.1.3.1;COFACTOR:Name=Fe(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29033; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Name=Zn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29105; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Name=Co(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:48828; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Note=Binds 1 divalent metal cation per subunit. Active withFe(2+), and probably also with Mn(2+), Zn(2+) and Co(2+).{ECO:0000250};SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000250}.MISCELLANEOUS: According to some authors, RPEL1 is a RPE retrogeneon chromosome 2 which is likely to be functional.{ECO:0000305|PubMed:16201836}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ribulose-phosphate 3-epimerase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

