<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P19623">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_4c501bb73b934b4813e3ff2e096792de" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Spermidine synthase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_SRM_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P19623" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPEE_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPDSY</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SRML1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Putrescine aminopropyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPS1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.5.1.16</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SRM</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SPEE_HUMAN Reviewed; 302 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ra.cs.uni-tuebingen.de/software/KEGGtranslator/EC25116.eref</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_6723</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P19623_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the production of spermidine from putrescineand decarboxylated S-adenosylmethionine (dcSAM). Has a strongpreference for putrescine as substrate, and has very low activitytowards 1,3-diaminopropane. Has extremely low activity towardsspermidine. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17585781}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=putrescine + S-adenosyl 3-(methylsulfanyl)propylamine =H(+) + S-methyl-5&apos;-thioadenosine + spermidine;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:12721, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:17509,ChEBI:CHEBI:57443, ChEBI:CHEBI:57834, ChEBI:CHEBI:326268;EC=2.5.1.16; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:17585781};ACTIVITY REGULATION: The activity is thought to be regulatedmainly by the availability of decarboxylated S-adenosylmethionine.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=20 uM for putrescine {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17585781};KM=0.9 uM for S-adenosylmethioninamine{ECO:0000269|PubMed:17585781};PATHWAY: Amine and polyamine biosynthesis; spermidinebiosynthesis; spermidine from putrescine: step 1/1.SUBUNIT: Homodimer or homotetramer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17585781}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the spermidine/spermine synthase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_003123</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference81701</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

