 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the phosphorylation of D-glucose to D-glucose6-phosphate using ADP as the phosphate donor. GDP and CDP canreplace ADP, but with reduced efficiency (By similarity).{ECO:0000250}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ADP + D-glucose = AMP + D-glucose 6-phosphate + H(+);Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11460, ChEBI:CHEBI:4167, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:61548, ChEBI:CHEBI:456215, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216;EC=2.7.1.147;COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU00584};Note=Binds 1 Mg(2+) ion per subunit. {ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU00584};PATHWAY: Carbohydrate degradation; glycolysis.{ECO:0000255|PROSITE-ProRule:PRU00584}.SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000250}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted {ECO:0000305}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=6;Name=1;IsoId=Q9BRR6-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q9BRR6-2; Sequence=VSP_013552;Name=3;IsoId=Q9BRR6-3; Sequence=VSP_013549;Name=4;IsoId=Q9BRR6-4; Sequence=VSP_013550, VSP_013551, VSP_013552;Name=5;IsoId=Q9BRR6-5; Sequence=VSP_013548, VSP_013553, VSP_013554;Name=6;IsoId=Q9BRR6-6; Sequence=VSP_035014;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ADP-dependent glucokinase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
