<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q96GX9">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_0857e232481a8058e47467367e40dd1a" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methylthioribulose-1-phosphate dehydratase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q96GX9" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_APIP_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTNB_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hAPIP</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">APIP</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTRu-1-P dehydratase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">4.2.1.109</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">APAF1-interacting protein</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the dehydration of methylthioribulose-1-phosphate (MTRu-1-P) into 2,3-diketo-5-methylthiopentyl-1-phosphate (DK-MTP-1-P). Functions in the methionine salvagepathway, which plays a key role in cancer, apoptosis, microbialproliferation and inflammation. May inhibit the CASP1-relatedinflammatory response (pyroptosis), the CASP9-dependent apoptoticpathway and the cytochrome c-dependent and APAF1-mediated celldeath. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15262985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:22837397,ECO:0000269|PubMed:23285211, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=5-methylsulfanyl-D-ribulose 1-phosphate = 5-methylsulfanyl-2,3-dioxopentyl phosphate + H2O;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:15549, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:58548,ChEBI:CHEBI:58828; EC=4.2.1.109; Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089};COFACTOR:Name=Zn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29105;Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116,ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089};Note=Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089};BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=9.3 uM for S-methyl-5-thio-D-ribulose 1-phosphate;Vmax=1.39 umol/min/mg enzyme;PATHWAY: Amino-acid biosynthesis; L-methionine biosynthesis viasalvage pathway; L-methionine from S-methyl-5-thio-alpha-D-ribose1-phosphate: step 2/6. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116,ECO:0000269|PubMed:23285211, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089}.SUBUNIT: Homotetramer (PubMed:24367089). Interacts with APAF1(PubMed:15262985). May interact with CASP1 (PubMed:22837397).{ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15262985,ECO:0000269|PubMed:22837397, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24367089}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15262985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23285211}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1; Synonyms=Long;IsoId=Q96GX9-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2; Synonyms=Short;IsoId=Q96GX9-3; Sequence=VSP_044403;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Isoform 1 is ubiquitously expressed. Isoform 2is expressed at lower levels and detected in heart, brain,pancreas, liver, placenta, skeletal muscle and kidney.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15262985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23285211}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the aldolase class II family. MtnBsubfamily. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03116}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_51074</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q96GX9_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_51074</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTNB_HUMAN Reviewed; 242 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_14725_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference101276</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_057041</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

