 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_1M9K_see-also</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_4846</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_1M9R_see-also</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Produces nitric oxide (NO) which is implicated invascular smooth muscle relaxation through a cGMP-mediated signaltransduction pathway. NO mediates vascular endothelial growthfactor (VEGF)-induced angiogenesis in coronary vessels andpromotes blood clotting through the activation of platelets.FUNCTION: Isoform eNOS13C: Lacks eNOS activity, dominant-negativeform that may down-regulate eNOS activity by forming heterodimerswith isoform 1.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H(+) + 2 L-arginine + 3 NADPH + 4 O2 = 4 H2O + 2 L-citrulline + 3 NADP(+) + 2 nitric oxide; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:19897,ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:15379,ChEBI:CHEBI:16480, ChEBI:CHEBI:32682, ChEBI:CHEBI:57743,ChEBI:CHEBI:57783, ChEBI:CHEBI:58349; EC=1.14.13.39;COFACTOR:Name=heme; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:30413;COFACTOR:Name=FAD; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57692;Note=Binds 1 FAD.;COFACTOR:Name=FMN; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:58210;Note=Binds 1 FMN.;COFACTOR:Name=(6R)-L-erythro-5,6,7,8-tetrahydrobiopterin;Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:59560;Note=Tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4). May stabilize the dimeric form ofthe enzyme.;ACTIVITY REGULATION: Stimulated by calcium/calmodulin. Inhibitedby NOSIP and NOSTRIN. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11149895,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12446846}.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. Interacts with NOSIP and NOSTRIN. Interactswith HSP90AB1 (PubMed:23585225). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11149895,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12446846, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23585225}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cell membrane. Membrane, caveola. Cytoplasm,cytoskeleton. Golgi apparatus. Note=Specifically associates withactin cytoskeleton in the G2 phase of the cell cycle; which isfavored by interaction with NOSIP and results in a reducedenzymatic activity.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=P29474-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=eNOS13C;IsoId=P29474-2; Sequence=VSP_042625, VSP_042626;Note=Lacks eNOS activity.;Name=eNOS13B;IsoId=P29474-3; Sequence=VSP_045495, VSP_045496;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Platelets, placenta, liver and kidney.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:7515611}.PTM: Phosphorylation by AMPK at Ser-1177 in the presence ofCa(2+)-calmodulin (CaM) activates activity. In absence of Ca(2+)-calmodulin, AMPK also phosphorylates Thr-495, resulting ininhibition of activity (By similarity). Phosphorylation of Ser-114by CDK5 reduces activity. {ECO:0000250,ECO:0000269|PubMed:16126727, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20213743}.DISEASE: Note=Variation Asp-298 in NOS3 may be associated withsusceptibility to coronary spasm. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11740345,ECO:0000269|PubMed:9737779}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the NOS family. {ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Wikipedia; Note=Nitric oxide synthase entry;URL=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitric_oxide_synthase&quot;;WEB RESOURCE: Name=SeattleSNPs;URL=&quot;http://pga.gs.washington.edu/data/nos3/&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
