 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of serinefrom carbohydrates. The reaction mechanism proceeds via theformation of a phosphoryl-enzyme intermediates.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12777757}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + O-phospho-L-serine = L-serine + phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:21208, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:33384,ChEBI:CHEBI:43474, ChEBI:CHEBI:57524; EC=3.1.3.3;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12213811,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12777757, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + O-phospho-D-serine = D-serine + phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:24873, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:35247,ChEBI:CHEBI:43474, ChEBI:CHEBI:58680; EC=3.1.3.3;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12213811,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12777757, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819};COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819};Note=Binds 1 Mg(2+) ion per subunit.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Inhibited by calcium ions.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819}.PATHWAY: Amino-acid biosynthesis; L-serine biosynthesis; L-serinefrom 3-phospho-D-glycerate: step 3/3.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12213811,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12777757, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15291819}.DISEASE: Phosphoserine phosphatase deficiency (PSPHD)[MIM:614023]: An autosomal recessive disorder that results inpre- and postnatal growth retardation, moderate psychomotorretardation and facial features suggestive of Williams syndrome.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:14673469}. Note=The disease is caused bymutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the HAD-like hydrolase superfamily. SerBfamily. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P78330_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SERB_HUMAN Reviewed; 225 AA.</bp:comment>
